{"book":19,"chapter":2,"context":{"chapter":2,"title":"The LORD's Anointed King","summary":"Nations plot against the LORD and his anointed king, but God laughs, installs his king on Zion and calls him 'my Son.'","background":"A royal psalm, probably used when a new Davidic king was crowned; it has no title, but Acts 4:25 attributes it to David. 'Anointed' is Hebrew mashiach, 'messiah.' The New Testament applies it to Jesus (Acts 13:33; Hebrews 1:5).","customs":[{"term":"Kiss the Son","verses":"2:12","note":"Kissing a ruler, or his hand or feet, was a sign of homage and submission."},{"term":"A potter's vessel","verses":"2:9","note":"Clay pots shattered beyond repair. Egyptian rulers even smashed pottery inscribed with enemies' names as a symbolic curse."}],"watchFor":["Four speakers: the nations, the LORD, the king, and the psalmist (vv. 1–12).","'Thou art my Son; this day have I begotten thee' (v. 7)."],"connections":["Acts 4:25-26","Acts 13:33","Hebrews 1:5","2 Samuel 7:14"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["לָמָּה","lamah","H4100","HR/Pi","<to> why?"],["רָגְשׁוּ","rageshu","H7283","HVqp3cp","do they plot"],["גוֹיִם","goyim","H1471","HNcmpa","nations"],["וּלְאֻמִּים","ule'umim","H3816","HC/Ncmpa","and peoples"],["יֶהְגּוּ","yehgu-","H1897","HVqi3mp","do they devise?"],["רִיק","rik","H7385","HNcmsa","vanity"]],"x":[[44004025,44004026,33],[66017014,66017014,18],[19046006,19046006,15],[19021011,19021011,13],[19083004,19083008,12],[40021038,40021038,7],[44017005,44017006,7],[42022022,42022023,6],[19018042,19018042,5],[23008009,23008009,5]],"xn":15},"2":{"w":[["יִתְיַצְּבוּ","yityatzevu","H3320","HVti3mp","they take their stand"],["מַלְכֵי","malkhei-","H4428","HNcmpc","[the] kings of"],["אֶרֶץ","'eretz","H776","HNcfsa","[the] earth"],["וְרוֹזְנִים","veroznim","H7336","HC/Vqrmpa","and rulers"],["נוֹסְדוּ","nosdu-","H3245","HVNp3cp","they seat themselves"],["יָחַד","yachad","H3162","HNcmsa","together"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["ו